Track 3: Vera’s Circular Kiln
- Story & Context: Scene folklore claims that on the final night before Swiss bailiffs permanently welded the facility's airlocks shut, an itinerant glass artisan named Vera dragged a kerosene drum furnace into the center of the accelerator target chamber and began blowing delicate glass whistles for every raver still dancing. As the exhaust fans sputtered out and the tunnel grew dense with the hot, sweet scent of paraffin wax and ozone, twenty clubbers grabbed spare celesta mallets and pounded out a breathless 112 BPM polyrhythm that rolled continuously through the curved concrete banking. When police finally breached the heavy blast doors at noon, the hall was deserted except for three hundred glowing, cooling glass bells hanging from cables, vibrating in sympathetic harmony as the automated PA system blasted the triumphant hook, "Spin the light until the ring breaks wide!" into the empty room. To this day, ravers claim that pressing an ear against the Jura pasture drainage grates lets you hear the distant, happy ringing of that final track.
